  "description": "VESVOG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H158 Cl1 O24 S8 Tb5 3+,3(Cl1 1-),2(C2 H6 O1 S1),2(C6 H14). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.610-5.388 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.90-172.88°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C104H158ClO24S8Tb5·3Cl·2(C2H6OS)·2(C6H14). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Tb(III).",
